# Minerva Searcher
Hi, seems like you've stumbled upon this small tool I made.

This is a simple bash script that I created in order to simplify my process of retrieving and downloading games on Minerva Archive.
Since the torrent was a multifile and it has thousands of games.

---

## How to use
1. Download Aria2c
```
Sudo apt install aria2
```
2. Download the Torrent file and place it on the same folder of the .sh
3. run the script!
```
chmod +x MinervaSearch.sh
./MinervaSearch.sh
```

I have only tried to use this for Minerva Torrent for PSP, I'm not sure if it will work on general Torrent multifile, but assume it doesn't.

### Disclaimer

This tool is a general-purpose command-line utility built for managing, searching, and selectively downloading multi-file `.torrent` archives via `aria2c`. 

